LIMITATION variants are deliberately different models, not alternative no-go route families.
LIMITATION P0 and P1 already fail on the frozen baseline; overlap-one is recorded only as a distinct control, not a pass-to-fail mutation.
LIMITATION B7 mutates the envelope predicate with a synthetic elapsed value; it does not waste time or memory to force an actual envelope failure.
LIMITATION direct packet quadrature is a diagnostic cross-check; the analytic overlap and midpoint first-moment identities carry the proof.
LIMITATION ideal margins and variants use only the frozen pulse, path and dwells; no width or protocol parameter search was performed.
